===A5_S2_D3===
// item next to the river
Noelle: What happened?! #portrait:NoelleSad
Second Critter: We were hiding in tree!
Second Critter: Friend… fell…
Narrator: It starts choking up, about to cry from worry. 
Amelia: Noelle! #portrait:AmeliaHostile
Noelle: You get Clara, I’ll grab him! #portrait:NoelleAngry
Narrator: You step into the river without thinking twice, feeling the water freeze you up to your chest. The critter you’re looking for is clinging onto a strip of rivergrass, eyes shut tight.
Noelle: Hold on! #portrait:NoelleMask
Narrator: You wade over carefully, making sure to feel the ground before putting your weight on it. 
Narrator: The current grows more chaotic as your walking disturbs it. The critter almost loses its grip, until…
Noelle: Got you! #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Narrator: You wade to shore with the shivering critter in your arms. It buries itself into your top further, not daring to look until its back on solid ground.
Clara: There you are! Oh my gosh, are you both okay?! #portrait:Clara
Narrator: You belatedly realize that your entire outfit is soaked. 
Noelle: Well… we’re unharmed. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: There’s another critter stuck on a tree. I’ll get him and come back. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Narrator: Once you’re sat down with a towel over you and a change of clothes, you learn that Clara found one critter hiding in Kiara’s garden, and with the three you met, that accounts for them all.
Clara: <i>Never</i> go near the river again, you hear me? #portrait:Clara
Narrator: The critter swept away by the water and its accomplice who was with it in the tree, bow their heads and nod.
Narrator: Now that it’s over, you feel a little bad…
Noelle: They probably didn’t realize the river was so near. #portrait:NoelleSmallSmile
Noelle: And they’ve learned their lesson. So it’s fine, right? #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Narrator: Clara sighs, taking a deep breath.
Clara: Right. Say thank you to Amelia and Noelle. #portrait:Clara
Cotton critters: Thank you…
Narrator: With that out of the way, you finally let Clara know the initial reason you were searching for her.
Clara: Oh, Rowan! He’s probably the best fabric maker we’ve ever seen. #portrait:Clara
Clara: He works day in, day out, spinning, weaving, cutting and creating one of the most valuable things we produce in the village… <i>but</i>… #portrait:Clara
Amelia: But? #portrait:AmeliaSilly
Clara: He has a bit of a reputation for being… hard to reason with. #portrait:Clara
Clara: Well, it’s more of ‘hard to ask a favor from,’ but that’s just because he’s usually overworked, and even more stressed at the moment from making flood supplies. #portrait:Clara
Noelle: Right, he makes the tents, and probably clothes, blankets… #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: Clara smiles, glad that you understand.
Clara: Still, you’ll never know until you try. #portrait:Clara
Clara: In return for saving these little guys, I’ll give you a bit of fabric — then all he’ll have to do is assemble them for your sail. #portrait:Clara
Amelia: Won’t he need the dimensions and design? #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Clara: Oh, don’t worry about it. The Ichthyos and Krakenfolk use boats too, even if they’re just for fishing. #portrait:Clara
Clara: I’ll come with you. His workshop is just north of the village — you can’t miss it. #portrait:Clara
